cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, and cite the associated article once published."
type: software
title: "Source-Grouped Evaluation of Temporal Stacking for Seismic Phase Picking with Three-Component Data"
version: "source-verified-v2"
abstract: >
  Corrected source-verified evaluation of seismic temporal stacking on one
  fixed STEAD split, with recovered waveform identities, 106 checkpoints,
  fresh inference replay and conditional numerical audits. The PhaseNet-style
  baseline has a P advantage; primary S method differences remain unresolved.
  Historical development exposure prevents independent confirmation.
  No existing release DOI archives this corrected repository state.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rcw3712/ICNN_MetaPicker_Curated_STEAD_MATLAB"
keywords:
  - seismic phase picking
  - P-wave
  - S-wave
  - STEAD
  - stacking ensemble
  - meta-learning
  - CNN
  - TCN
  - deep learning
  - MATLAB
  - seismology
  - source-level validation
  - data leakage
